<p>I have paid attention to modern SCP theory. A goodly percent of submitted SCP entries are rejected for being too similar to other skips. If I had a dollar for every time I have heard &quot;overdone&quot;, &quot;cliche&quot;, or &quot;we already have one of those&quot; when we down vote articles then I could take a nice vacation. We have guides that specifically state that we don't want copied ideas as new skips. Maybe I am confused or overreacting but I fail to see how this gets a pass when other articles that do the same thing don't and we castigate the authors for it.</p>

