<p>I would say, based on your &quot;Blue Pool&quot; example above, that you are missing the point of why some skips get downvoted as &quot;cliche&quot; or &quot;too much like SCP-XXX&quot; and others don't. You are 100% right that if an SCP tells the same story as an earlier one, or is easily recognized as &quot;X from Y, SCP-ified&quot; people will downvote, <em>because you repeated the same story</em>. Not because the objects are similar. This is a common misconception. Your &quot;Blue Pool&quot; would get downvoted, because it is telling the same story with some minor details changed.</p>
<p>In other words: Want to make a cliched item work? Tell a story about it that the reader is not expecting.</p>

