					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dankaar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1790336); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1790336&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608411039" alt="dankaar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1790336)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dankaar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1790336); return false;" >dankaar</a></span> <span class="odate time_1452123923 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Jan 2016 23:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2435547">
									

<p>Well, if we consider the poster thinking of a truly infinite universe&#8230;</p>
<p>&#8230; the answer is going to be &quot;the chances of Milo writing a SCP into real life are infinity to one&quot;. Or we shouldn't even bet on it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Detailed&nbsp;explanation</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Gimme&nbsp;all&nbsp;the&nbsp;Tylenol&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;pharmacy&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;headache&nbsp;I&nbsp;just&nbsp;got!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>To start, we first assume that there are an infinite amount of universes, with infinite variations of how they came to be, physical properties, etc. Then, we start narrowing it down to just universes that, let's say, formed life. That cuts the universes we need to consider in half. However, that's still infinity, it's just one half as large as all the infinite universes. Then we narrow it down to ones where humans exist, ones where Earth exists and so on until we nestle into the much-smaller-yet-still-infinite group of universes where both we and the SCP verse resides in. While all this doesn't have any direct bearing on the question, we need it so we can keep in mind that there are actually larger and smaller infinities.</p>
<p>The question if Milo does write a SCP here, we have the following possibilites: Milo successfully writes in SCPS to our universe or Milo doesn't write them in.</p>
<p>What's that? Only 50-50 you say? No, actually, it's not.</p>
<p>While there's an infinite amount of ways where Milo can write a SCP into Real Life, it's a much smaller infinity where they don't. Because under the codifer &quot;Milo doesn't write in SCPs,&quot; there are the infinities in categories of everything from &quot;Bob down the street from Milo is the only one who will do it&quot; to &quot;This universe will never have a SCP in it&quot; to &quot;SCPs will never reach Earth&quot; to &quot;Milo never correctly writes in the one that would cross over&quot;, as well as all the various other infinities included in that prevent Milo from successfully writing in a SCP.</p>
<p>Yes, they all count because we're comparing them against one codifier- where Milo successfully writes a SCP into real-life. For Milo to succeed, this universe MUST be connected to the SCP verse, AND it must be possible to write a SCP into the real life, AND Milo is the one to do it. So long as one of those three is not true, it won't happen. And considering all the universes that are not connected to the SCP verse (like just about all mass media, to start with), all the universes where a SCP never interacts with Earth, all the universes where humans never meet a SCP, all the universes where it is not possible to write a SCP into real life, all the ones where Milo is not the one to do it, et cetera, that's a much larger infinity than the specific scenario that we defined.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

